 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 667009,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Consider the following example. Line 13 executes and <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">SubClass()</code> is called. Which line does control flow move to?\n<pre class=\"python line-numbering\" data-lang=\"python\">class SuperClass:\n&nbsp;&nbsp;def __init__(self):\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;self.feat_1 = 1\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;self.feat_2 = \"\"\n\n&nbsp;&nbsp;def bc_display(self):\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;print(f\"Superclass: {self.feat_2}\")\n\nclass SubClass(SuperClass):\n&nbsp;&nbsp;def dc_display(self):\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;print(f\"Subclass: {self.feat_2}\")\n\ndc_1 = SubClass()\n</pre>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1330000,
     "content_html": "2",
     "correctness": "1.0",
     "feedback_html": "<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">SubClass'</code>s <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">__init__()</code> is not explicitly defined, so <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">SuperClass'</code>s <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">__init__()</code> is executed."
    },
    {
     "id": 1330001,
     "content_html": "10",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "dc_1 should be instantiated using the available __init__()."
    },
    {
     "id": 1330002,
     "content_html": "<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">Error</code>",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "When the subclass's __init__() is not explicitly defined, the superclass's __init__() is called."
    }
   ],
